.......","..Q.....",".....Q..",".Q......","......Q."],["....Q...",".......Q","...Q....","Q.......","......Q.",".Q......",".....Q..","..Q....."],[".....Q..","Q.......","....Q...",".Q......",".......Q","..Q.....","......Q.","...Q...."],[".....Q..",".Q......","......Q.","Q.......","..Q.....","....Q...",".......Q","...Q...."],[".....Q..",".Q......","......Q.","Q.......","...Q....",".......Q","....Q...","..Q....."],[".....Q..","..Q.....","Q.......","......Q.","....Q...",".......Q",".Q......","...Q...."],[".....Q..","..Q.....","Q.......",".......Q","...Q....",".Q......","......Q.","....Q..."],[".....Q..","..Q.....","Q.......",".......Q","....Q...",".Q......","...Q....","......Q."],[".....Q..","..Q.....","....Q...","......Q.","Q.......","...Q....",".Q......",".......Q"],[".....Q..","..Q.....","....Q...",".......Q","Q.......","...Q....",".Q......","......Q."],[".....Q..","..Q.....","......Q.",".Q......","...Q....",".......Q","Q.......","....Q..."],[".....Q..","..Q.....","......Q.",".Q......",".......Q","....Q...","Q.......","...Q...."],[".....Q..","..Q.....","......Q.","...Q....","Q.......",".......Q",".Q......","....Q..."],[".....Q..","...Q....","Q.......","....Q...",".......Q",".Q......","......Q.","..Q....."],[".....Q..","...Q....",".Q......",".......Q","....Q...","......Q.","Q.......","..Q....."],[".....Q..","...Q....","......Q.","Q.......","..Q.....","....Q...",".Q......",".......Q"],[".....Q..","...Q....","......Q.","Q.......",".......Q",".Q......","....Q...","..Q....."],[".....Q..",".......Q",".Q......","...Q....","Q.......","......Q.","....Q...","..Q....."],["......Q.","Q.......","..Q.....",".......Q",".....Q..","...Q....",".Q......","....Q..."],["......Q.",".Q......","...Q....","Q.......",".......Q","....Q...","..Q.....",".....Q.."],["......Q.",".Q......",".....Q..","..Q.....","Q.......","...Q....",".......Q","....Q..."],["......Q.","..Q.....","Q.......",".....Q..",".......Q","....Q...",".Q......","...Q...."],["......Q.","..Q.....",".......Q",".Q......","....Q...","Q.......",".....Q..","...Q...."],["......Q.","...Q....",".Q......","....Q...",".......Q","Q.......","..Q.....",".....Q.."],["......Q.","...Q....",".Q......",".......Q",".....Q..","Q.......","..Q.....","....Q..."],["......Q.","....Q...","..Q.....","Q.......",".....Q..",".......Q",".Q......","...Q...."],[".......Q",".Q......","...Q....","Q.......","......Q.","....Q...","..Q.....",".....Q.."],[".......Q",".Q......","....Q...","..Q.....","Q.......","......Q.","...Q....",".....Q.."],[".......Q","..Q.....","Q.......",".....Q..",".Q......","....Q...","......Q.","...Q...."],[".......Q","...Q....","Q.......","..Q.....",".....Q..",".Q......","......Q.","....Q..."]]}],"solution":"class Solution:\n    def solveNQueens(self, n: int) -> List[List[str]]:\n        res = []\n        cols_used = set()\n        diag1 = set()  # r - c\n        diag2 = set()  # r + c\n        placement = []  # placement[r] = column of the queen in row r\n\n        def backtrack(r: int) -> None:\n            if r == n:\n                res.append([\".\" * c + \"Q\" + \".\" * (n - c - 1) for c in placement])\n                return\n            for c in range(n):\n                if c in cols_used or (r - c) in diag1 or (r + c) in diag2:\n                    continue\n                cols_used.add(c); diag1.add(r - c); diag2.add(r + c)\n                placement.append(c)\n                backtrack(r + 1)\n                placement.pop()\n                cols_used.remove(c); diag1.remove(r - c); diag2.remove(r + c)\n\n        backtrack(0)\n        return res\n","approach":"**Key insight: one queen per row, so the search is over columns, and the three kinds of attack lines (column, r - c diagonal, r + c diagonal) can each be tracked with a set for O(1) conflict checks.**\n\n**Algorithm.** `backtrack(r)`: if `r == n` render the board from the per-row column list. Otherwise for each column `c` not in `cols`, `r - c` not in `diag1`, `r + c` not in `diag2`: add all three, push `c`, recurse to `r + 1`, then undo. Return the collected boards.\n\n**Why it works.** Two queens attack along a column iff they share `c`, along a diagonal iff they share `r - c` or `r + c`. Since rows are distinct by construction, those three sets capture every conflict, and the search enumerates every conflict-free assignment exactly once.\n\n**Common mistakes:** scanning previously placed queens for conflicts (O(n) per check, still passes but misses the point); mixing up the two diagonal keys; rendering the board with the wrong row/column orientation; forgetting to undo one of the three sets.\n\n**Interview follow-ups:** Only count the solutions (N-Queens II)? (same search, increment a counter; bitmasks for the three sets make it very fast.) Exploit symmetry? (only try the first n/2 columns in row 0 and mirror, handling the middle column for odd n.) How large can n get? (the count grows super-exponentially; backtracking is practical to roughly n = 15.)","complexity":{"time":"O(n!) upper bound on the search tree","space":"O(n) for sets and recursion, excluding output"},"similar":["n-queens-ii","sudoku-solver","permutations"],"number":99,"starter":"class Solution:\n    def solveNQueens(self, n: int) -> List[List[str]]:\n        pass\n"}